{"title":"Career roadmap — Audit Assistant","role":"Audit Assistant","summary":"An Audit Assistant supports internal, statutory, tax, and financial audits by checking financial records, testing transactions, reconciling accounts, preparing working papers, identifying control gaps, and supporting senior auditors.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"B.Com General"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Com graduate, the strongest route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accounting fundamentals","Audit basics","Excel + Tally/ERP","GST/Tax","Internal Controls","Audit tools","CA/ACCA/CIA pathway"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","What to focus on"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Accounting, auditing, taxation, Excel, Tally/ERP, GST, financial statements, audit documentation"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Internal controls, risk-based auditing, ERP audits, data analytics, internal/statutory audit"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Audit analytics, continuous auditing, automation, compliance, risk management"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"AI-enabled audit, continuous assurance, forensic analytics, GRC and audit leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Accounting foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial accounting"},{"text":"Journal entries"},{"text":"Ledgers"},{"text":"Trial balance"},{"text":"Bank reconciliation"},{"text":"Depreciation"},{"text":"Accruals and provisions"},{"text":"Inventory accounting"},{"text":"Accounts receivable/payable"},{"text":"Profit & Loss"},{"text":"Balance Sheet"},{"text":"Cash-flow statements"},{"text":"Basic taxation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MS Excel"},{"text":"TallyPrime"},{"text":"Basic accounting softwar